  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read the hub first",
      "items": [
        "AI Software Factory is the premise: humans write specs and tests, agents implement until the tests pass; the spec is the asset, the code disposable.",
        "Verification Bottleneck is the consequence: the constraint moves from writing code to verification, review and security, and the human/AI review boundary is recalibrated each model generation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Where verification lives",
      "items": [
        "Advisory and Deterministic Controls: a skill makes violations rare; only a hook, sandbox or PR review makes them close to impossible.",
        "Tiered Autonomy: freedom scales with deviation, environment, change size and trust earned, and always stops at the production gate.",
        "AI-Native SDLC: six stages rebuilt as a loop chained by committed markdown artifacts that are both handoff and audit trail."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where the tensions are",
      "items": [
        "Prototype or plan: Just-in-Time Planning's contested claim says prototypes replace design docs; AI-Native SDLC implements nothing without an accepted plan.md, checked by a hook. Stage or disagreement is unsettled.",
        "Spec as asset vs agents that drift: the factory has humans only define and judge; the hub and the controls say agents drift plausibly and must not weaken their own tests. Implicit, not stated.",
        "Spend tokens or save them: Token Efficiency calls cost per task compatible with fleets and a burn-tokens posture, but files no claim for it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Sourcing",
      "items": [
        "Weakest: the factory's no-hand-written-code repo, low confidence, secondhand and greenfield-only.",
        "Nearly every other claim is supported at medium confidence on Anthropic or vendor-collected sources; one consultant is the only outside voice. Read supported as not yet contested."
      ]
    }
  ]
}